      "message": "feat(ui): a refused generation shows the moves it had built as a ghost\n\n#261 part 3. A refusal raised with a path in hand now carries that path\nas a display-only diagnostic ghost, on the carrier part 2 built for the\nrefusal's spot: GenError::Ghosted -> CommandError::MachiningGhost ->\nState::feedback_ghost. The viewport draws it dashed in the dimmed gouge\ncolour, without chevrons, and it retires with the refusal sentence. It\nis never cached on the operation: the op still has no toolpath, the post\nrefuses it as ungenerated and the simulation has nothing to play.\n\nAdopters: the ladders' centre-cutting refusal (pocket/adaptive/offset,\ncontour, contour chain, slot, bore, circular, the 3-D ladder) and the\nplunge law's audit of a finished path (finish and multiaxis guards,\nRotary Offset's bar audit, the posed audit, the facer's air entry).\nRotary Offset's wrap-space ladder drops its ghost. Capped at 100k moves;\nnon-finite ghosts are dropped. The script/MCP generate error names the\nghost's move count.\n\nFixes #261\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
